WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.357
In this code example, we create a Sale class.

00:00:03.357 --> 00:00:07.912
The class stores three pieces of information: item, price, and quantity.

00:00:07.912 --> 00:00:11.412
These are attributes of the object.

00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:13.632
Then we define a method called total.

00:00:13.632 --> 00:00:19.647
This method multiplies the price by the quantity and returns the result.

00:00:19.647 --> 00:00:24.497
After defining the class, we create one Sale object for a notebook.

00:00:24.497 --> 00:00:26.412
The price is 12.50 and the quantity is 4.

00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:31.222
Then we print the item name, the quantity, and the total.

00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:34.172
Before running the code, calculate the total in your head.

00:00:34.172 --> 00:00:39.257
Twelve dollars and fifty cents times four should be fifty dollars.

00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:43.722
Run the cell and confirm the output.

00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:45.967
Then change the price or quantity and run it again.

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:52.872
Notice that the total method automatically uses the updated values stored in the object.

00:00:52.872 --> 00:00:56.979
This is the power of combining data and behavior in a class.
